Those singing hooligans really got my motor running.

272
00:13:51,860 --> 00:13:53,440
Sure, sure. Enjoy.

273
00:13:53,450 --> 00:13:55,680
I mean, get it back to me when you can, or...

274
00:13:55,680 --> 00:13:56,960
you know what, actually, you keep it.

275
00:13:56,960 --> 00:13:58,350
It's just going to be my gift to you.

276
00:13:58,350 --> 00:13:59,590
- Thank you. - Bye.

277
00:13:59,950 --> 00:14:02,270
Wait... Where'd the painting go?

278
00:14:02,750 --> 00:14:04,020
It's right over there.

279
00:14:04,920 --> 00:14:06,030
Why?

280
00:14:07,370 --> 00:14:09,760
I have no idea. That is weird.

281
00:14:12,690 --> 00:14:14,080
- You hate it. - No.

282
00:14:14,080 --> 00:14:17,050
No, no. It's just, it's a little big.

283
00:14:17,130 --> 00:14:19,110
- I feel like an idiot. - No, come on, you're not an idiot.

284
00:14:19,110 --> 00:14:20,620
Look, just help me put it back up.

285
00:14:20,620 --> 00:14:22,710
Why? So you can just take it down when I leave?

286
00:14:22,710 --> 00:14:25,430
- I don't need your pity. - Oh, Amy, come on...

287
00:14:25,440 --> 00:14:27,690
I'm just glad I didn't go for the sculpture.

288
00:14:32,380 --> 00:14:35,020
Ah, the spoils.

289
00:14:35,040 --> 00:14:37,190
I see why Victors love them.

290
00:14:38,400 --> 00:14:39,660
I'm happy for you, Sheldon.

291
00:14:39,670 --> 00:14:42,930
But I have to admit I'm going to miss sharing an office with you.

292
00:14:42,930 --> 00:14:44,160
Oh, of course you are.

293
00:14:44,160 --> 00:14:46,300
Feel free to drop by any time.

294
00:14:46,300 --> 00:14:48,190
- Thank you. - Yeah. Call first.

295
00:14:54,970 --> 00:14:56,740
Oh. Hello.

296
00:14:58,880 --> 00:15:00,050
Professor Rothman.

297
00:15:00,060 --> 00:15:01,840
This isn't your office anymore.

298
00:15:01,840 --> 00:15:03,250
You're retired.

299
00:15:03,950 --> 00:15:07,690
I think the word you're looking for is... "Invisible."

300
00:15:13,480 --> 00:15:15,170
I came to say I'm sorry.

301
00:15:15,170 --> 00:15:16,250
Don't bother.

302
00:15:16,250 --> 00:15:19,010
- Oh, Amy, please. - I'm so humiliated.

303
00:15:19,010 --> 00:15:20,700
I sat there the whole time that we were watching "Grease,"

304
00:15:20,710 --> 00:15:22,990
- thinking you liked the painting. - I know.

305
00:15:22,990 --> 00:15:25,100
I was a fool from "Summer Lovin'" To the very last

306
00:15:25,100 --> 00:15:27,150
"Rama lama lama ke ding a de dinga a dong."

307
00:15:29,440 --> 00:15:30,640
You're right. You're absolutely right.

308
00:15:30,640 --> 00:15:31,840
I should have been honest with you

309
00:15:31,840 --> 00:15:34,450
and told you the gift was too much.

310
00:15:34,550 --> 00:15:36,070
Yes, too much.

311
00:15:36,070 --> 00:15:38,380
Because our friendship is fundamentally asymmetrical.

312
00:15:38,510 --> 00:15:40,630
I clearly like you more than you like me.

313
00:15:41,560 --> 00:15:43,500
I don't think you can put a number on

314
00:15:43,500 --> 00:15:44,940
how much one person likes another.

315
00:15:44,940 --> 00:15:47,490
I bought you a painting that's 12 square feet in area.

316
00:15:47,490 --> 00:15:48,770
There's a number.

317
00:15:49,820 --> 00:15:50,590
Amy, come on...

318
00:15:50,590 --> 00:15:52,180
If you don't like feet, you can try dollars.

319
00:15:52,190 --> 00:15:54,100
The painting set me back three grand.

320
00:15:55,310 --> 00:15:57,590
Three gr... Oh, my God!

321
00:15:58,800 --> 00:16:00,100
Look, look, Amy,

322
00:16:00,100 --> 00:16:02,790
all you need to know is, you are my friend

323
00:16:02,790 --> 00:16:04,860
and I don't want to lose you out of my life.

324
00:16:05,170 --> 00:16:08,030
I'm sorry, I'm just having trouble believing you right now.

325
00:16:11,400 --> 00:16:12,250
Grab your hammer.

326
00:16:12,260 --> 00:16:14,310
No. Damage is done.

327
00:16:16,450 --> 00:16:18,570
Okay, look, I didn't want to say this,

328
00:16:18,570 --> 00:16:21,640
but the real reason I took the painting down was...

329
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:24,880
because it made Bernadette very jealous.

330
00:16:27,040 --> 00:16:28,280
Oh, my goodness,

331
00:16:28,280 --> 00:16:30,680
how could I have not seen that?

332
00:16:30,790 --> 00:16:31,440
The painting is

333
00:16:31,440 --> 00:16:33,520
a constant reminder that of the three of us,

334
00:16:33,520 --> 00:16:35,420
she is the least cool.

335
00:16:37,880 --> 00:16:40,480
Yeah, that's... that's what it is, so...

336
00:16:40,780 --> 00:16:42,120
You have such a good heart.

337
00:16:42,120 --> 00:16:43,680
Yeah... I try.

338
00:16:44,990 --> 00:16:46,160
Come on.

339
00:16:46,350 --> 00:16:47,880
Whoa, whoa, where are we going?

340
00:16:47,880 --> 00:16:49,510
We're going to go put this painting back up in your apartment.

341
00:16:49,510 --> 00:16:51,540
- Well, what about Bernadette? - Oh, screw her.

342
00:16:51,540 --> 00:16:53,480
She's just lucky we let her hang out with us.

343
00:17:17,220 --> 00:17:18,410
What are you doing?

344
00:17:18,740 --> 00:17:20,570
I'm trying to raise the temperature in here

345
00:17:20,570 --> 00:17:22,660
before my nipples tear through my shirt.

346
00:17:24,600 --> 00:17:27,030
Why don't you just turn up the thermostat?

347
00:17:27,030 --> 00:17:28,400
Aha! Good question.

348
00:17:28,400 --> 00:17:30,930
It turns out the thermostat for my new office

349
00:17:30,930 --> 00:17:33,320
isn't in my new office. No. It's next door,

350
00:17:33,320 --> 00:17:35,300
in Professor Davenport's office,

351
00:17:35,300 --> 00:17:39,120
who is currently enjoying the hot flashes associated with menopause.

352
00:17:40,630 --> 00:17:42,150
Why is there a hole here?

353
00:17:42,150 --> 00:17:44,250
Why is there a hole in my new office?

354
00:17:44,250 --> 00:17:46,440
I've narrowed it down to two possibilities:

355
00:17:46,440 --> 00:17:48,340
"There was something in the wall

356
00:17:48,340 --> 00:17:50,540
that someone outside the wall wanted,"

357
00:17:50,540 --> 00:17:52,090
or the more disturbing,

358
00:17:52,090 --> 00:17:55,100
"There was something in the wall that wanted out."

359
00:17:56,580 --> 00:17:58,740
Well, at least you finally got a window that opens.

360
00:17:58,750 --> 00:17:59,420
That's nice.

361
00:17:59,420 --> 00:18:01,540
Is it? Listen.

362
00:18:03,590 --> 00:18:04,610
What, you don't like wind chimes?

363
00:18:04,610 --> 00:18:06,520
No, I hate them, but it gets worse.

364
00:18:10,100 --> 00:18:12,880
- There it is. - The bird?

365
00:18:12,880 --> 00:18:15,740
It's completely out of tune with the wind chimes.

366
00:18:16,760 --> 00:18:17,460
So?

367
00:18:17,460 --> 00:18:18,640
You don't get it, do you?

368
00:18:18,640 --> 00:18:19,770
That's a mockingbird.

369
00:18:19,770 --> 00:18:21,940
Mockingbirds can change their song,

370
00:18:21,940 --> 00:18:24,420
which means he's out of tune on purpose.

371
00:18:25,160 --> 00:18:26,830
He's mocking me.

372
00:18:27,800 --> 00:18:30,670
Oh dear. There it is again. Do you feel it?

373
00:18:30,670 --> 00:18:32,050
The growing realization

374
00:18:32,050 --> 00:18:33,930
that you are one wacky bastard? Yep.

375
00:18:34,890 --> 00:18:36,600
No. The vibration.

376
00:18:36,600 --> 00:18:38,940
We are directly underneath the geology lab,

377
00:18:38,940 --> 00:18:41,320
and they're running their confounded sieve shakers again.

378
00:18:41,320 --> 00:18:42,430
Hey, gravel monkeys,

379
00:18:42,430 --> 00:18:45,390
if you need to shake rocks, try jiggling your heads around!

380
00:18:46,570 --> 00:18:47,760
Sheldon, relax.

381
00:18:47,760 --> 00:18:49,070
How can I relax?

382
00:18:49,070 --> 00:18:51,000
My nervous system is being stretched out

383
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:54,690
like the strings of a harp and plucked by holes and birds

384
00:18:54,690 --> 00:18:57,170
and wind and the low-hanging scrotum

385
00:18:57,170 --> 00:18:59,390
of the difficult-to-evict Professor Rothman.

386
00:19:01,410 --> 00:19:02,110
If you're not happy,

387
00:19:02,110 --> 00:19:04,260
why don't you just let Kripke have the office?

388
00:19:04,260 --> 00:19:05,470
Wait, and let him win?

389
00:19:05,480 --> 00:19:07,280
Do I look crazy to you?

390
00:19:07,770 --> 00:19:09,040
We're trying to think down here,

391
00:19:09,040 --> 00:19:11,640
you geode-loving feldspar jockeys!

392
00:19:11,930 --> 00:19:13,180
And you...

393
00:19:13,180 --> 00:19:15,700
the notes are C, D, E, G and A.

394
00:19:15,700 --> 00:19:18,570
You pick one or I am chopping down that tree!

395
00:19:24,300 --> 00:19:25,650
How's that?

396
00:19:25,920 --> 00:19:27,230
Little higher on the right.

397
00:19:28,490 --> 00:19:30,070
- Now? - Little more.

398
00:19:30,070 --> 00:19:31,470
No. That's got it.

399
00:19:34,250 --> 00:19:36,940
Yeah, okay. That's, uh, that's good.

400
00:19:38,180 --> 00:19:40,310
I'll let you in on a little secret.

401
00:19:40,690 --> 00:19:42,800
Originally we were painted nude.

402
00:19:49,820 --> 00:19:51,850
But I had him add clothes, 'cause I thought

403
00:19:51,850 --> 00:19:55,490
it was an unnecessary challenge to our heterosexuality.

404
00:19:57,750 --> 00:19:58,920
Yeah, good call.

405
00:20:00,290 --> 00:20:01,630
But if you ever change your mind, all it would take

406
00:20:01,630 --> 00:20:04,510
is some warm, soapy water and a couple of sponges.

407
00:20:06,670 --> 00:20:08,970
- You're talking about the painting, right? - Sure.

408
00:20:14,940 --> 00:20:17,230
Help! Somebody help!

409
00:20:20,880 --> 00:20:21,910
What happened?

410
00:20:21,910 --> 00:20:25,470
I was trying to see what was in here and my head got stuck.

411
00:20:26,610 --> 00:20:27,840
Why would you do that?

412
00:20:27,840 --> 00:20:30,570
It's called scientific curiosity!

413
00:20:31,740 --> 00:20:33,190
Now go get butter.

414
00:20:34,470 --> 00:20:35,380
Hang in there.

415
00:20:35,380 --> 00:20:36,990
I'll be right back.

